# What `gcloud run deploy --source .` uploads to Cloud Build.
#
# **Inherit .gitignore, then exclude the tracked things the image has no use for.** That order
# matters and the first line is the important one.
#
# An earlier version of this file was a standalone exclude list, on the reasoning that a missed
# *source* path fails the build loudly while a missed *exclude* only makes it slow. That was wrong:
# a missed exclude crashed the upload outright —
#
#     ERROR: gcloud crashed (PermissionError): [Errno 13] Permission denied:
#            '.vs\Polson\FileContentIndex\13c4a26c-....vsidx'
#
# — because Visual Studio holds its index open, and gcloud reads every file it is not told to skip.
# `.vs` was already gitignored; the standalone list simply never asked. Inheriting `.gitignore`
# covers that whole class: IDE state, build output, virtualenvs, anything a tool writes and git was
# already told to ignore.
#
# It is safe to inherit, because anything tracked in git is by definition not gitignored, and
# everything the build needs is tracked.

#!include:.gitignore

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tracked, and still not wanted in the image.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `.gitignore` cannot help with these: they are committed on purpose and would be uploaded.

# Third-party books and source, read by people and never by the image. 1.4 GB.
reference/

# Documentation and tests: neither is needed to run the service.
docs/
tests/

# NOT `*.md`. An earlier version had it, and it would have broken the image at runtime rather than
# at build: `Polson.CLI.csproj` carries
#     <EmbeddedResource Include="ProjectTemplate\**\*.md" />
# so the 39 workflow templates — every instructions.md, brief.md and roles/*.md — are *source*.
# Excluding them would have produced a CLI that builds cleanly and then generates empty projects.
# Root-level markdown is a few KB; the bulk is `reference/` and `docs/`, both already excluded.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Belt and braces.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Restated even though `.gitignore` covers them, so that a change there cannot quietly start
# shipping a secret or an IDE lock file.
.git/
.vs/
.idea/
.vscode/
*.env
**/appsettings.json
python/
python-adk/
**/__pycache__/
